  "system": {
    "description": "<p>Originally distributed as a bot-targeting virus by prankster hackers, DDR (&ldquo;Dance Dance Robot&rdquo;) triggers impulses in your motor control circuits. The effect makes your shell &ldquo;dance&rdquo; in jerky, automated movements. Pleasure receptors are also activated so that dancing &mdash; and movement of any kind &mdash; feels fantastic. Variants invoke different motions and styles. While dancing, you suffer a -20 modifier to other actions. You can override the dancing with a WIL Check. Non-embodied infomorphs feel the need to dance, but are otherwise unaffected.</p>",
    "reference": "Eclipse Phase Second Edition p. 333",
